<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
    For the Mac App Store build (-DCARVE_APP_STORE=ON) only. The Developer ID
    disk image is signed with Carve.entitlements instead; see LICENSING.md.

    The store requires the App Sandbox. Inside it the app can reach its own
    container and nothing else, so what it needs beyond that is asked for
    here, and it is not much:

      * the files the user points at in an open or save panel, read and
        written: songs, samples, SoundFonts, voicebanks, and exports.
      * the right to keep that access across launches, as security-scoped
        bookmarks. A song is a list of paths to samples picked on some
        earlier day, and without this every one of them would be out of
        reach the next time the app opened. See src/app/SandboxAccess.h.

    What is deliberately absent:

      * disable-library-validation. The other entitlements file has it so
        that a plugin host can load other vendors' AU/VST3 bundles. This
        build hosts none, and the store does not take that exception.
      * audio input. The app never records audio. MIDI input needs no
        entitlement.
      * network. The app talks to nobody.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.files.bookmarks.app-scope</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
